						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</aside>

			<article class="col-span-full grid gap-8 lg:col-span-8 xl:gap-12 [&_h2[id]]:scroll-mt-20">
				<div class="rounded-lg bg-background p-10 text-foreground" data-card>
					<div class="prose max-w-none font-medium text-pretty lg:text-lg">
						<h2>Key takeaways</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Local China-based support with global reach</li>
							<li>Faster, real-time communication and issue resolution</li>
							<li>Flexible billing aligned to multiple legal entities</li>
							<li>Reduced operational and compliance risk</li>
							<li>Scalable model supporting future growth</li>
						</ul>
						<hr />
						<p>Managing a global IP portfolio at Alibaba requires precision, speed, and strong coordination. With thousands of annuity cases annually, even small inefficiencies created significant operational pressure. Time zone delays and rigid workflows limited responsiveness. Alibaba needed a partner that could match its scale and complexity.</p>
						<p>Before working with RWS, Alibaba relied on a global supplier model that lacked local presence in China. Communication was mainly handled by email, often resulting in next-day responses. In urgent situations, these delays caused concern and increased risk for the IP process team, particularly when managing time-sensitive annuity payments.</p>
						<h2>The challenge of scale and complexity</h2>
						<p>Alibaba Group operates through more than 30 legal entities worldwide, many with independent financial systems. The previous supplier could not support flexible billing or customized workflows, creating inefficiencies across renewals and payments.</p>
						<p>In addition, the supplier’s lack of a China-based team meant language barriers, time zone gaps, and slower feedback loops. As Alibaba’s global patent portfolio expanded, these challenges increasingly impacted productivity and confidence.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div>
